-count calculation. For nonnegative values, you must sort by ascending bit count and descending decimal value on a tie, using (count_ones(x), -x).\\n\\n6. **Combine Results**\\n   - Combine the sorted negative and non-negative integers into a single list.\\n   - Return the combined list.\\n\\n7. **Edge Cases**\\n   - Handle an empty input list.\\n   - Handle a list with only negative integers.\\n   - Handle a list with only non-negative integers.\\n\\n8. **Complexity Considerations**\\n   - Ensure the counting of binary ones is efficient.\\n   - Ensure the sorting step is efficient.\\n\\n9. **Test Cases**\\n\\n   - Implement the checklist above directly and use the existing task validation suite.\\n\\n### Example Code Snippet\\n\\n   - Implement the checklist above directly and use the existing task validation suite.\\n\\n"}'}]
